content.text:
Found the root cause. Here's the comparison:

**Old file** — [TaskDocuments.tsx:558-563](HHHHQA/src/globalComponents/TaskDocuments.tsx:558) (`LoadAllSiteTasks`):
```js
if (isRadimadeDrivenContext && props?.AllSiteTasks?.length == 0) {
    // Do not bind sub-docs with partial/fallback task data before Radimade completes.
    return;
}
```
If the task hierarchy (`AllSiteTasks`) isn't loaded yet, it just bails out — `filterTagDoc()` never runs until real data is available. No result is ever committed against incomplete data.

**New file** — [TaskDocuments.tsx:701-709](hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-Directory/documents/TaskDocuments.tsx:701), same guard, but with a new branch added on top of it (only for Portfolio Profile):
```js
if (isRadimadeDrivenContext && props?.AllSiteTasks?.length == 0) {
    // Portfolio Profile sub-expand: still run filter against master hierarchy alone.
    if (props?.isPortfolioProfile && subDocsRequestedRef.current) {
        AllSitesAllTasksRef.current = [];
        filterTagDoc();     // <-- runs the filter with an EMPTY task list
        return;
    }
    return;
}
```

`filterTagDoc()` builds the "Relevant Sub-item Documents" list (`findtagdoc`) partly from `AllSitesAllTasksRef.current` — it walks each task/sprint/cycle row's `SmartDocument` field to find docs tagged at the task level, not just docs tagged directly on the Portfolio item. When this branch fires, that task list is forced to `[]`, so **every document only tagged via a child Task/Sprint/Cycle (not directly on the Portfolio) gets silently dropped** from the sub-item table. Then it immediately calls `setSubDocsLoading(false)` — so the UI reports "done" with that incomplete result, and nothing re-runs the filter later once the real task data actually arrives (the effect that would normally re-trigger on data-ready is skipped for Portfolio Profile — [line 243](hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-Directory/documents/TaskDocuments.tsx:243), `deferSubDocsUntilOpen` returns early).

This matches your screenshots exactly:
- **"All Relevant Documents"** (built from `findtagactualdoc`, tagged directly to the Portfolio) — unaffected, correctly empty in both old and new.
- **"Relevant Sub-item Documents"** (built from `findtagdoc`, needs the task hierarchy) — new SPA shows 12, old shows 15 — the 3 missing docs are the ones tagged only via child Task/Sprint/Cycle rows, dropped because this branch ran the filter against an empty task list.

This code only exists in the new SPA (added as part of the "load sub-item docs on accordion expand" lazy-load feature) — the old classic page has no equivalent, which is why it never hits this bug.

Want me to fix it — i.e., have this branch just wait (like the old code) instead of finalizing against an empty array?

