Analysis done — no changes made. Here's what I found, read-only:

## Root cause #1 — confirmed: "Key Portfolio Items" empty on SPA nav

This is a **field-selection mismatch** between two different REST queries, not a stale-cache issue.

The "Key Portfolio Items" display doesn't actually come from the `Portfolios` field directly. In `ProjectManagementMain.tsx` around [line 991-1037](HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectManagement/components/ProjectManagementMain.tsx:991), there's a second enrichment pass that **always** runs (seed or not) and **overwrites** whatever was set earlier:

```js
fetchedProject.taggedPortfolios = [];
lookupIds(fetchedProject?.PortfoliosId).forEach((item) => {
    MasterListData?.map((portfolio) => {
        if (portfolio?.Id == item) {
            fetchedProject?.taggedPortfolios?.push(portfolio);
            ...
        }
    });
});
...
if (fetchedProject?.taggedPortfolios != undefined) {
    smartPortfoliosData = fetchedProject.taggedPortfolios   // this is what actually renders
}
```

This depends entirely on `fetchedProject.PortfoliosId` — the **raw lookup-ID field** (e.g. `{results: [123]}`), not the expanded `Portfolios/Id, Portfolios/Title` object.

- The **cold single-item fetch** ([line 707](HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectManagement/components/ProjectManagementMain.tsx:707)) explicitly selects `"PortfoliosId"` alongside `"Portfolios/Id", "Portfolios/Title"`.
- The **shared/cached query** that feeds Project Overview's table (and therefore the seed handed to PXC Profile via `PxcProfileNavLink` → `setPxcSeed`) is `MASTER_TASK_UNIFIED_SELECT` in [globalCommon.tsx:2669-2691](hhhh-shared-ui/src/HHHH-SP-Code/services/globalCommon.tsx:2669) — it selects `Portfolios/Id, Portfolios/Title, Portfolios/PortfolioStructureID` but **never selects bare `PortfoliosId`**.

So when you navigate via the SPA (seed path), `fetchedProject.PortfoliosId` is `undefined` → `lookupIds()` returns `[]` → `taggedPortfolios` stays `[]` → "Key Portfolio Items" renders empty. A hard refresh always goes through the cold fetch, which has the field, so it works.

This is a genuinely clean, isolated fix candidate: add `"PortfoliosId"` to `MASTER_TASK_UNIFIED_SELECT`.

## Root cause #2 — likely, not fully confirmed: missing breadcrumb ancestry

The breadcrumb ([line 7738-7753](HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectManagement/components/ProjectManagementMain.tsx:7738)) needs `Masterdata.Parent.Parent.Id/.Title` — a two-level-deep nested object. There's a resolution step at [line 983-988](HHHHWorkspace/src/pages/projectManagement/components/ProjectManagementMain.tsx:983) that replaces the clicked item's shallow `Parent: {Id, Title}` stub with the full matching row found in `AllFlatProject`. That only resolves **one level** for the clicked item itself — whether the grandparent shows up correctly depends on whether *that* resolved parent row (X19) already had its own `.Parent` fully resolved when `AllFlatProject` was built from the shared/seeded data. I haven't traced far enough to say definitively whether that transitively works or not — it's plausible this has the same "shared query built the tree with only shallow one-level Parent stubs" flavor as root cause #1, but I'm not certain, and want to actually trace `AllFlatProject`'s construction before claiming it.

Want me to keep tracing #2 to full certainty, or is #1 (which I'm confident about) enough to hand to Cursor now, with #2 flagged as "needs more digging"?

